  "term": "remission",
  "definition": "In this packet, remission refers to the post-treatment phase when a patient has finished active care for localized breast cancer and moves into ongoing monitoring, including a remission consultation and personalized follow-up. The packet does not provide a broader general definition of the term beyond this care context.",
